diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4451f30..dc80fe8 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -26,6 +26,8 @@ The **Tier lists** tab contains **Truck** and **Region Difficulty** sub-tabs. Th
 
 ANK MK38 Civilian (`ank_mk38_ht`) is included in the base truck catalog even though its XML is stored under `_dlc/dlc_6` without a truck entitlement entry. It appears in Tier lists → Truck → Unsorted until ranked, and shares that assignment with Truck properties. Its tier is independent of the regular ANK MK38.
 
+Tire randomization has its own saved **Easy / Normal / Hard** selector in Randomizer → Truck-Randomization → Obtainable, independent of Region progression difficulty. Every new placement rolls independently. The first region in the finalized order requests 99% Highway and 1% All-terrain in every mode, even if it is ranked S or is the only region. Later tire weights blend progression position (80%) with region difficulty (up to 20%, introduced gradually), interpolating from Highway toward better categories. Easy grants better tires sooner; Hard keeps weaker tires in the mix. In the final S-tier region, Highway / All-terrain / Offroad / Mudtires odds are 0/5/25/70% on Easy, 3/12/40/45% on Normal, and 10/25/35/30% on Hard. Truck compatibility can change the actual category to the nearest supported one; the smallest supported size and first variant are still used. Detailed logs show the position, region tier, tire difficulty, requested odds and any fallback without naming replacement trucks. Existing saved/pending assignments stay fixed; use Regions-Trucks reset before rerandomizing them under different settings. Changing tire difficulty does not change the finalized region order or apply map files. The former unedited default tire-rule note is updated when loaded; custom notes and empty lists are preserved.
+
 Run it from the repository root with:
 
 ```powershell
